l:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rog chos brtson</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P10017</idno><idno type="APIS">4242</idno></person><person xml:id="person4243"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'ban dkon mchog rdo rje</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">འབན་དཀོན་མཆོག་རྡོ་རྗེ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'ban</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">b+han</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'b+han</persName><birth notBefore="1000-01-01" notAfter="1110-12-31">after 1000 before 1110</birth><death notBefore="1026-01-01" notAfter="1190-12-31">after 1026 before 1190</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P10013</idno><idno type="APIS">4243</idno><note type="comment">Contemporaneous with rGya dmar ba (ID: 3834) and sTag pa kha che (ID: 4265) ([MGPRHX73]: 54, n. 18)</note></person><person xml:id="person4291"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">ngur smrig pa dar ma snying po</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ངུར་སྨྲིག་པ་དར་མ་སྙིང་པོ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">ngur mig pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dar ma snying po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">ngur smrig pa chen po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">ngur dmigs pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rong gi dge bshes ngur dmig pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">brang ti dar ma snying po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">brang ti dar snying</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'brang</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">ngur mig</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'ur smrig</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">brang ti</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rdu</persName><birth notAfter="1085-12-31">before 1085</birth><death notBefore="1105-01-01">after 1105</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P10011</idno><idno type="APIS">4291</idno><note type="comment">We follow Stearns ([RA3FK3BK]: 245, n. 173 and n. 176) in assuming that Ngur smrig pa is the same person as Brang ti Dar ma snying po, a foremost figure in the transmission of the Abhidharma in Tibet.&#13;
